    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "quantized-inference",
        "title": "Normalize FP32 biases for dense and EXL3 layers",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Linear.load_fp16 passes loaded biases into LinearFP16; convert_exl3 later obtains that stored bias through get_bias_tensor and forwards it to LinearEXL3. Casting in LinearFP16 normalizes this upstream path, while casting independently in LinearEXL3 also handles biases loaded directly from quantized storage.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_119a504d7463413daf4bf5466213a851",
              "call_1f4d8fce89a344de9760989d88af9c8b",
              "call_b49f156460cb46e99400c0636b6b7401"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "This is FP32 input acceptance through downcasting, not FP32 bias preservation. Dense forward adds the stored bias to its half-precision output; EXL3 forward casts its result to the stored bias dtype before addition. None and existing half biases bypass the new conversion.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_41033f96b7da4be4b8f8939105faa310",
              "call_b3507c645f0049afb182f3aa701daeda",
              "call_b49f156460cb46e99400c0636b6b7401",
              "call_1f4d8fce89a344de9760989d88af9c8b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "A standard-library scalar illustration rounded FP32 0.10000000149011612 to binary16 0.0999755859375, showing the precision tradeoff of normalization. This did not execute repository code.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_83f00cf39cb34386bcb003cc55fc69f9"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "EXL3 also loses its general bias-dtype assertion: non-FP32, non-half biases now pass this constructor check unchanged. The patch does not establish their downstream compatibility. LinearFP16_torch is unchanged.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_b49f156460cb46e99400c0636b6b7401",
              "call_41033f96b7da4be4b8f8939105faa310"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [],
    "summary": "Accept FP32 biases in dense and EXL3 constructors by converting them to FP16, removing the EXL3 bias assertion that could interrupt conversion."
  },
